 persons, racialized persons, persons with disabilities, women and LGBTQIA2S+ persons. The University is committed to creating and maintaining an accessible, barrier-free work environment. The University is also committed to working with applicants with disabilities requesting accommodation during the recruitment, assessment and selection processes. Applicants with disabilities may contact vra.affairesprofessorales@uottawa.ca to communicate the accommodation need. All qualified candidates are encouraged to apply; however, Canadians and permanent residents will be given priority. Prior to May 1, 2022, the University required all students, faculty, staff, and visitors (including contractors) to be fully vaccinated against Covid-19 as defined in Policy 129 \u2013 Covid-19 Vaccination. This policy was suspended effective May 1, 2022 but may be reinstated at any point in the future depending on public health guidelines and the recommendations of experts."}, "https://uottawa.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/uOttawa_External_Career_Site/job/Ottawa-ON/APTPUO---Winter-2027---EDU-4102---A00---Equity--Diversity-and-Inclusion-in-Education_JR39301": {"title": "APTPUO - Winter 2027 - EDU 4102 - A00 - Equity, Diversity and Inclusion in Education", "description": "Posted: 2026-09-23\nPart time\n\nPosting Reason: New Position Location: Main Campus Academic Period: 2027 Winter Semester Faculty: Facult\u00e9 d'\u00e9ducation / Faculty of Education Academic Unit: Formation \u00e0 l\u2019enseignement (Fac. Education) Course Title: Equity, Diversity and Inclusion in Education Course Code: EDU 4102 Section: A00 Course Description: Examination of theories of equity in relation to sexism, racism, ableism, and other social inequalities; current trends in universal design and implications in diverse and inclusive settings. Posting limited to: Professeur \u00e0 temps-partiel r\u00e9gulier / Regular Part-Time Professor Date Posted (YYYY/MM/DD): 2026/09/23 Applications must be received BEFORE (YYYY/MM/DD): 2026/09/23 Expected Enrolment: 50 Approval date: 2026/09/23 Number of credits: 3 Work Hours: 39 Hourly Rate: Enseignement / Teaching: $239.47 (2024-2025) The academic year starts on September 1 and ends on August 31. These rates do not included vacation pay nor statutory pay. These rates will be applied until a new collective agreement is ratified. Retro will be paid after the ratification. Course type: B Posting type: R\u00e9gulier / Regular Language of instruction: Anglais | English Competence in second language: Passive Course Schedule: Mercredi | Wednesday 17:30-20:30 - - Videoconference during a given time slot. Students are required to be online at the same time. Requirements: Master's degree in education required; preference will be given to a doctorate in education. - At least one of the following: Recent experience teaching full-time in a school or school board administration, including two years of implementing the Ontario curriculum (subject: French) with a specialist qualification (subject: French) or - Current and referenced research record (subject: French), or - Recent comprehensive examination (doctorate) (subject: French); - Demonstrated knowledge of the current Ontario curriculum for French and Ontario Ministry of Education documents related to French. - Demonstrated ability to apply the standards of practice and code of ethics of the Ontario College of Teachers. - The university may consider experience or qualifications equivalent to those listed above. Additional Information and/or Comments: An acceptable level of education and/or experience could be viewed as being equivalent to the educational required and/or demonstrated experience. If you are invited to continue the selection process, please notify us of any adaptive measures you might require. Information you send us will be handled respectfully and in complete confidence. Employees are required under provincial law to successfully complete all mandatory legislated training. The list of training may be modified by provincial law. The hiring process will be governed by the current APTPUO collective agreements; you can click here for the main unit , here for the OLBI unit , or here for the Toronto/Windsor unit to find out more. The University of Ottawa embraces diversity and inclusion in the workplace. We are passionate about our people and committed to employment equity. We foster a culture of respect, teamwork and inclusion, where collaboration, innovation, and creativity fuel our quest for research and teaching excellence. While all qualified persons are invited to apply, we welcome applications from qualified Indigenous persons, racialized persons, persons with disabilities, women and LGBTQIA2S+ persons. The University is committed to creating and maintaining an accessible, barrier-free work environment. The University is also committed to working with applicants with disabilities requesting accommodation during the recruitment, assessment and selection processes. Applicants with disabilities may contact vra.affairesprofessorales@uottawa.ca to communicate the accommodation need. All qualified candidates are encouraged to apply; however, Canadians and permanent residents will be given priority. Prior to May 1, 2022, the University required all students, faculty, staff, and visitors (including contractors) to be fully vaccinated against Covid-19 as defined in Policy 129 \u2013 Covid-19 Vaccination. This policy was suspended effective May 1, 2022 but may be reinstated at any point in the future depending on public health guidelines and the recommendations of experts."}, "https://uottawa.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/uOttawa_External_Career_Site/job/Ottawa-ON/APTPUO---Winter-2027---EDU-4502---A00---quit--diversit-et-inclusion-en-ducation_JR39302": {"title": "APTPUO - Hiver 2027 - EDU 4502 - A00 - \u00c9quit\u00e9, diversit\u00e9 et inclusion en \u00e9ducation", "description": "Posted: 2026-09-23\nPart time\n\nPosting Reason: New Position Location: Main Campus Academic Period: 2027 Winter Semester Faculty: Facult\u00e9 d'\u00e9ducation / Faculty of Education Academic Unit: Formation \u00e0 l\u2019enseignement (Fac. Education) Course Title: \u00c9quit\u00e9, diversit\u00e9 et inclusion en \u00e9ducation Course Code: EDU 4502 Section: A00 Course Description: Examen des th\u00e9ories de l'\u00e9quit\u00e9 en relation avec le sexisme, le racisme, le capacitisme et d'autres in\u00e9galit\u00e9s sociales ; tendances actuelles en mati\u00e8re de conception universelle et implications dans des environnements diversifi\u00e9s et inclusifs. Posting limited to: Professeur \u00e0 temps-partiel r\u00e9gulier / Regular Part-Time Professor Date Posted (YYYY/MM/DD): 2026/09/23 Applications must be received BEFORE (YYYY/MM/DD): 2026/10/24 Expected Enrolment: 50 Approval date: 2026/09/23 Number of credits: 3 Work Hours: 39 Hourly Rate: Enseignement / Teaching: $239.47 (2024-2025) The academic year starts on September 1 and ends on August 31. These rates do not included vacation pay nor statutory pay. These rates will be applied until a new collective agreement is ratified. Retro will be paid after the ratification. Course type: B Posting type: R\u00e9gulier / Regular Language of instruction: Fran\u00e7ais | French Competence in second language: Passive Course Schedule: Jeudi | Thursday 14:30-17:30 - - Vid\u00e9oconf\u00e9rence pendant une tranche horaire donn\u00e9e. La pr\u00e9sence en ligne synchrone des \u00e9tudiant.es est exig\u00e9e. Requirements: Un niveau \u00a0jug\u00e9 \u00e9quiv. pourrait suppl\u00e9er aux exigences d'\u00e9ducation et/ou d'exp\u00e9rience requises. Si on vous invite \u00e0 poursuivre les \u00e9tapes du processus de s\u00e9lection, veuillez nous aviser de tout besoin n\u00e9cessitant des mesures d'adaptation. Les renseignements communiqu\u00e9s seront trait\u00e9s avec respect et confidentialit\u00e9. Les employ\u00e9(e)s sont tenus(e) par la loi provinciale de mener \u00e0 bien des formations obligatoires. La liste des formations peut \u00eatre modifi\u00e9e par une loi provinciale. PhD de pr\u00e9f\u00e9rence et exp\u00e9rience d\u2019enseignement au cycle interm\u00e9diaire-sup\u00e9rieur. Connaissance d\u00e9montr\u00e9e du Curriculum de l'Ontario actuel et des documents du minist\u00e8re de l'\u00c9ducation de l'Ontario Capacit\u00e9 prouv\u00e9e \u00e0 appliquer les Normes d'exercice de la profession et le Code de d\u00e9ontologie de l'Ordre des enseignantes et des enseignants de l'Ontario. Au moins un parmi : Exp\u00e9rience r\u00e9cente en enseignement \u00e0 temps plein dans une \u00e9cole ou en administration au sein d'un conseil scolaire, incluant deux ans de mise en oeuvre du Curriculum de l'Ontario avec une qualification sp\u00e9cialiste ou Dossier de recherche actuel et arbitr\u00e9, ou Examen de synth\u00e8se (Ph.D) r\u00e9cent; L'Universit\u00e9 peut consid\u00e9rer l'exp\u00e9rience ou des qualifications \u00e9quivalentes \u00e0 celles mentionn\u00e9es ci-haut. Additional Information and/or Comments: An acceptable level of education and/or experience could be viewed as being equivalent to the educational required and/or demonstrated experience. If you are invited to continue the selection process, please notify us of any adaptive measures you might require. Information you send us will be handled respectfully and in complete confidence. Employees are required under provincial law to successfully complete all mandatory legislated training. The list of training may be modified by provincial law. The hiring process will be governed by the current APTPUO collective agreements; you can click here for the main unit , here for the OLBI unit , or here for the Toronto/Windsor unit to find out more. The University of Ottawa embraces diversity and inclusion in the workplace. We are passionate about our people and committed to employment equity. We foster a culture of respect, teamwork and inclusion, where collaboration, innovation, and creativity fuel our quest for research and teaching excellence. While all qualified persons are invited to apply, we welcome applications from qualified Indigenous persons, racialized persons, persons with disabilities, women and LGBTQIA2S+ persons. The University is committed to creating and maintaining an accessible, barrier-free work environment. The University is also committed to working with applicants with disabilities requesting accommodation during the recruitment, assessment and selection processes. Applicants with disabilities may contact vra.affairesprofessorales@uottawa.ca to communicate the accommodation need. All qualified candidates are encouraged to apply; however, Canadians and permanent residents will be given priority. Prior to May 1, 2022, the University required all students, faculty, staff, and visitors (including contractors) to be fully vaccinated against Covid-19 as defined in Policy 129 \u2013 Covid-19 Vaccination. This policy was suspended effective May 1, 2022 but may be reinstated at any point in the future depending on public health guidelines and the recommendations of experts."}, "https://uottawa.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/uOttawa_External_Career_Site/job/Ottawa-ON/Assistant-Professor_JR39197": {"title": "Assistant Professor", "description": "Posted: 2026-09-23\nFull time\n\nPosting Reason: New Position Job Family: Academic Leadership and Faculty Union affiliation: APUO Faculty/Department: Department of Modern Languages and Literatures_FT Campus: Main Campus Date Posted (YYYY/MM/DD): 2026/09/23 Applications must be received BEFORE (YYYY/MM/DD): The Department of Modern Languages and Literatures at the University of Ottawa invites applications for a full-time, tenure-track Assistant Professor or Associate Professor (subject to qualifications and experience) position in Arab Studies. We seek a dynamic researcher whose work advances critical, interdisciplinary approaches to research questions in the Arabic-speaking world. The ideal candidate will contribute to existing expertise at the University of Ottawa by undertaking research initiatives that examine contemporary cultural questions and social issues in regions of the Arabic-speaking world, and they will have experience in the field of Arabic as a Foreign Language (AFL). The candidate selected will also be considered for appointment to hold a Faculty of Arts Research Fellowship; for details on the Fellowship please see below. The intent of the Fellowship is to encourage interdisciplinary research and international collaborations regarding cultural dynamics and social change in the Arab societies, as well as among Arab-Canadian communities. This role may include developing partnerships, organizing seminars, supporting research initiatives, and fostering connections with academic, diplomatic, and community partners in Canada and abroad. The Univ\u0435rsity \u043ef Ott\u0430w\u0430 st\u0430nds \u043eut \u0430s \u0430 pr\u043emin\u0435nt high\u0435r educati\u043en instituti\u043en, r\u0435c\u043egnized b\u043eth nati\u043enally \u0430nd internati\u043enally, \u0430nd h\u043elds the title \u043ef the l\u0430rgest bilingual (Fr\u0435n\u0441h- English) univ\u0435rsity gl\u043ebally. Locat\u0435d \u043en the an\u0441estral, un\u0441eded l\u0430nds \u043ef the Ani\u0441hinab\u00e9-Alg\u043enquin p\u0435\u043eple in d\u043ewnt\u043ewn Ottaw\u0430, it plays a cruci\u0430l r\u043el\u0435 in enhancing th\u0435 \u0435c\u043en\u043emy, culture, and \u043everall quality \u043ef life in C\u0430nada\u2019s capital The \u0430nti\u0441ip\u0430ted start date f\u043er this p\u043esiti\u043en is July 1st, 2027. J\u043eb Titl\u0435: Assistant Pr\u043efess\u043er or Associate Professor. The rank is commensurate with experience. \u00a0 Areas of Expertise Candidates must demonstrate research and teaching expertise in one or more of the following subfields: Arts, Media, and Digital Cultures: Interdisciplinary study of classical and contemporary Arab cultural production across the Middle East and North Africa, including the use of computational methods to examine language, texts and culture, in a context of postcolonial realities and geopolitical change. Arab World, Migration, Diaspora, and Transnational Studies : Forced and voluntary displacement, border-crossing narratives, and global Arab identity networks. Middle East Studies : Broad contextual knowledge of the region\u2019s historical, geopolitical, linguistic, and socio-demographic complexities; Comparative Studies : Ability to place Arab societies and cultural production in conversation with global, transregional, or Western artistic movements. Imperialism, Colonialism, and Development : Critical frameworks evaluating power dynamics, postcolonial realities, and geopolitical shifts. Social change in Arab societies: Intersectional approaches that examine the dynamics of social change with respect to gender, identity, demographics, and the family in contemporary societies. Rank: Assistant or Associate Professor (Tenure-Track). The rank is commensurate with experience. Responsibilities: Duties include, in varying proportions: a) active research and knowledge mobilization program; b) teaching; c) recruitment and supervision of graduate students; d) service to the community. Develop research projects in Arab Studies; Leadership in the development of a transdisciplinary Arab Studies research initiative across the University; Coordinate the Department\u2019s Arabic Language and Culture section Teach undergraduate and graduate courses in Arab Studies in both French and English; Recruit and train graduate students. Term: T\u0435nure-Track p\u043esiti\u043en. Salary: The starting salary for an Assistant Professor is $99,377 (according to the scale in effect as of May 1, 2025). C\u043ensid\u0435rati\u043en f\u043er \u043ether ranks may \u043eccur under e\u0445c\u0435pti\u043enal c\u043enditi\u043ens. Ben\u0435fits: Th\u0435 University \u043ef Ott\u0430w\u0430 pr\u043evides an \u0435\u0445tensive benefits pa\u0441kage , which in\u0441lud\u0435s l\u043eng-t\u0435rm disability c\u043everage, basic life insurance, suppl\u0435m\u0435ntary h\u0435\u0430lth b\u0435nefits, a pensi\u043en pl\u0430n, \u043epti\u043enal lif\u0435 insurance, and r\u0435imbursement f\u043er r\u0435l\u043e\u0441ati\u043en e\u0445penses. Work location: Department of Modern Languages and Literatures, Faculty of Arts, University of Ottawa, 70 Laurier East Avenue, Ottawa, Ontario K1N 6N5 C\u043ent\u0430\u0441t (f\u043er inquiries): Dr. Luis Abanto, Chair, Department of Modern Languages and Literatures, University of Ottawa, email : llmdir@uottawa.ca Qualifications Education : Possess a doctorate (Ph.D.) by July 1, 2027, in Arab Studies, with demonstrated expertise in AFL pedagogy, Arabic and Comparative Literature, Middle East Studies, Arab Media/Cultural Studies, or a related discipline. Linguistic Fluency : Excellent communication skills in English and/or French. Active knowledge of Canada\u2019s two official languages (French and English) is a requirement for tenure. Native or near-native fluency in Modern Standard Arabic (MSA). Research Track Record : A demonstrated track record of research excellence, including peer-reviewed publications. Pedagogy : Demonstrated excellence or strong potential for teaching excellence in Arab Studies or related discipline. Arab Studies Research Fellowship The University of Ottawa aspires to create a dynamic research hub about transformations and innovations occuring in the countries of the Arab world and within the cultures of the Arab diaspora. To this end, the Faculty of Arts Research Fellowhship is open with respect to the field of Arab Studies \u2013 candidates with expertise in any of the themes outlined above will be considered. The person appointed to the Fellowship is expected to demonstrate commitment to innovative, ground-breaking research about cultural and social processes and change that affect Arab communities. This research fellowship is for an initial appointment of five years, with the possibility of renewal. The Fellowship comes with an annual research fund of $25,000. Additional funding will be available to support research activities of graduate students and postdoctoral fellows. The Fellowship is intended to support an exceptional scholar for whom Arab Studies is their primary research focus. D\u0435adline: Applic\u0430ti\u043ens r\u0435ceived by November 9, 2026 will be fully \u0441\u043ensider\u0435d; h\u043ew\u0435ver, th\u0435 p\u043esiti\u043en will rem\u0430in \u043epen until it is filled. Further details ab\u043eut academic c\u0430r\u0435\u0435rs can b\u0435 f\u043eund \u043enlin\u0435 . Applicati\u043ens must be submitted thr\u043eugh the University \u043ef Ottawa\u2019s c\u0430reer p\u043ertal , and \u043enly c\u043empl\u0435te submissi\u043ens will be evaluated. Pl\u0435as\u0435 submit the f\u043ell\u043ewing d\u043e\u0441uments in \u0430 single PDF: cover letter, curriculum vitae, two recent peer-reviewed publications, statement of research interests, and an example of a course syllabus. Following an initial review of applications, selected candidates will be invited to present their research to professors and students and asked to have three confidential letters of reference submitted directly by the referees. To learn more about our department, please visit: https://www.uottawa.ca/faculty-arts/department The University \u043ef Ott\u0430wa is committed t\u043e providing its academic community with a lead\u0435rship \u0430nd l\u0435arning envir\u043enment th\u0430t promot\u0435s equity, div\u0435rsity, and inclusi\u043en. As such, we strongly enc\u043eurag\u0435 appli\u0441ati\u043ens fr\u043em Indigen\u043eus pe\u043eples \u043ef Canada, visible min\u043erities, individu\u0430ls with dis\u0430bilities, w\u043emen, and \u0430ll qualifi\u0435d candidates with th\u0435 skills and kn\u043ewl\u0435dge t\u043e engag\u0435 c\u043enstructiv\u0435ly with c\u043emmunities that embrace equity, diversity and inclusion. Applic\u0430nts fr\u043em th\u0435se gr\u043eups are invited t\u043e fill out a \u0441\u043enfidential s\u0435lf-identifi\u0441\u0430ti\u043en questi\u043enn\u0430ir\u0435 wh\u0435n submitting th\u0435ir appli\u0441\u0430ti\u043ens. All qualified candidates are invited to apply; however, preference will be given to Canadians and permanent residents. When submitting your application, please indicate if you are legally entitled to work in Canada. Throughout the recruitment process, the University of Ottawa will provide accommodations to candidates with disabilities. If you are invited to proceed through the selection process, please notify us of any accommodation needs by writing to the Office of the Vice-Provost, Faculty Relations at vra.affairesprofessorales@uOttawa.ca . All information received will be treated confidentially. The University of Ottawa is proud of its more than 160-year tradition of bilingualism. Through its Official Languages and Bilingualism Institute, the University offers its employees, as well as their partners, the means to become bilingual. The University of Ottawa is committed to ensuring equity, diversity, and inclusion in the scholarly and leadership environments of our students, staff, and faculty. Accordingly, we strongly encourage applications from Indigenous Peoples in Canada, visible minorities members (racialized persons), persons with disabilities, women, as well as from all qualified candidates with the skills and knowledge to productively engage with equitable, diverse, and inclusive communities. Candidates who wish to be considered as a member of one or more designated groups are asked to complete the confidential Self-Identification Questionnaire, to be completed at the time of application. \u00a0 All qualified candidates are invited to apply; however, preference will be given to Canadians and permanent residents. When submitting your application, please indicate if you are legally entitled to work in Canada \u00a0 The University of Ottawa provides accommodations for applicants with disabilities throughout the recruitment process. If you are invited to proceed in the selection process, please notify us of any accommodations that you require by contacting the Office of the Vice-Provost, Faculty Relations by email at vra.affairesprofessorales@uottawa.ca . Any information you send us will be handled respectfully and in complete confidence. \u00a0 The University of Ottawa is proud of its 160-year tradition of bilingualism. Through its Official Languages and Bilingualism Institute, the University provides training to staff members and to their spouses in their second official language. \u00a0 Prior to May 1, 2022, the University required all students, faculty, staff, and visitors (including contractors) to be fully vaccinated against Covid-19 as defined in Policy 129 \u2013 Covid-19 Vaccination. This policy was suspended effective May 1, 2022 but may be reinstated at any point in the future depending on public health guidelines and the recommendations of experts."}, "https://uottawa.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/uOttawa_External_Career_Site/job/Ottawa-ON/APTPUO---Hiver-2027---PED3543-B100---VAL-APPRENTIS--L-LMENT_JR39298": {"title": "APTPUO - Hiver 2027 - PED3543 B100 - \u00c9VAL. APPRENTIS. \u00c0 L'\u00c9L\u00c9MENT.", "description": "Posted: 2026-09-23\nPart time\n\nPosting Reason: New Position Location: Main Campus Academic Period: 2027 Winter Semester Faculty: Facult\u00e9 d'\u00e9ducation / Faculty of Education Academic Unit: Formation \u00e0 l\u2019enseignement (Fac. Education) Course Title: \u00c9valuation des apprentissages \u00e0 l'\u00e9l\u00e9mentaire Course Code: PED 3543 Section: B100 Course Description: PED3543: \u00c9valuation des apprentissages \u00e0 l'\u00e9l\u00e9mentaire \u00c9tude des diff\u00e9rentes \u00e9tapes de l'\u00e9valuation scolaire. D\u00e9veloppement et analyse d'outils d'\u00e9valuation. \u00c9tude des contenus en lien avec les politiques du Minist\u00e8re de l'\u00c9ducation de l'Ontario. D\u00e9veloppement du jugement en \u00e9valuation des apprentissages. \u00c9tude de la nature, des fonctions et des finalit\u00e9s de l'\u00e9valuation. Veuillez noter que le cours est offert en personne Posting limited to: Professeur \u00e0 temps-partiel r\u00e9gulier / Regular Part-Time Professor Date Posted (YYYY/MM/DD): 2026/09/23 Applications must be received BEFORE (YYYY/MM/DD): 2026/10/24 Expected Enrolment: 45 Approval date: 2026/09/23 Number of credits: 3 Work Hours: 39 Hourly Rate: Enseignement / Teaching: $239.47 (2024-2025) The academic year starts on September 1 and ends on August 31. These rates do not included vacation pay nor statutory pay. These rates will be applied until a new collective agreement is ratified. Retro will be paid after the ratification. Course type: B Posting type: R\u00e9gulier / Regular Language of instruction: Fran\u00e7ais | French Competence in second language: Passive Course Schedule: Lundi | Monday 8:30-11:30 Mercredi | Wednesday 8:30-11:30 - Cours offert en personne Requirements: Exigences minimales: - Ma\u00eetrise en \u00e9ducation; La pr\u00e9f\u00e9rence sera donn\u00e9e \u00e0 un doctorat en \u00e9ducation portant sur l'\u00e9valuation des apprentissages. - Au moins un parmi : Exp\u00e9rience r\u00e9cente en enseignement \u00e0 temps plein dans une \u00e9cole ou en administration au sein d'un conseil scolaire incluant deux ans de mise en oeuvre du curriculum de l'Ontario au cycle p/m/i avec une qualification sp\u00e9cialiste au cycle p/m/i Dossier de recherche actuel et arbitr\u00e9 dans la mati\u00e8re du cours \u00e0 enseigner. Examen de synth\u00e8se (Ph.D.) r\u00e9cent dans la mati\u00e8re du cours \u00e0 enseigner. - Connaissance d\u00e9montr\u00e9e du contexte de l'Ontario en ce qui a trait \u00e0 la mati\u00e8re du cours \u00e0 enseigner. \u00a0- Capacit\u00e9 manifeste d'appliquer les Normes d'exercice de la profession et du Code de d\u00e9ontologie des\u00a0 enseignantes et enseignants de l'Ontario. Un niveau d'\u00e9ducation/d'exp\u00e9rience jug\u00e9 \u00e9quivalent pourrait suppl\u00e9er aux exigences d'\u00e9ducation et/ou d'exp\u00e9rience requises. Si nous vous invitons \u00e0 poursuivre les \u00e9tapes du processus de s\u00e9lection, veuillez nous aviser de tout besoin n\u00e9cessitant des mesures d'adaptation. Les renseignements communiqu\u00e9s seront trait\u00e9s avec respect et confidentialit\u00e9. Les employ\u00e9(e)s sont tenus(e) par la loi provinciale de mener \u00e0 bien des formations obligatoires. La liste des formations peut \u00eatre modifi\u00e9e par une loi provinciale. Additional Information and/or Comments: An acceptable level of education and/or experience could be viewed as being equivalent to the educational required and/or demonstrated experience. If you are invited to continue the selection process, please notify us of any adaptive measures you might require. Information you send us will be handled respectfully and in complete confidence. Employees are required under provincial law to successfully complete all mandatory legislated training. The list of training may be modified by provincial law. The hiring process will be governed by the current APTPUO collective agreements; you can click here for the main unit , here for the OLBI unit , or here for the Toronto/Windsor unit to find out more. The University of Ottawa embraces diversity and inclusion in the workplace. We are passionate about our people and committed to employment equity. We foster a culture of respect, teamwork and inclusion, where collaboration, innovation, and creativity fuel our quest for research and teaching excellence. While all qualified persons are invited to apply, we welcome applications from qualified Indigenous persons, racialized persons, persons with disabilities, women and LGBTQIA2S+ persons. The University is committed to creating and maintaining an accessible, barrier-free work environment. The University is also committed to working with applicants with disabilities requesting accommodation during the recruitment, assessment and selection processes. Applicants with disabilities may contact vra.affairesprofessorales@uottawa.ca to communicate the accommodation need. All qualified candidates are encouraged to apply; however, Canadians and permanent residents will be given priority. Prior to May 1, 2022, the University required all students, faculty, staff, and visitors (including contractors) to be fully vaccinated against Covid-19 as defined in Policy 129 \u2013 Covid-19 Vaccination. This policy was suspended effective May 1, 2022 but may be reinstated at any point in the future depending on public health guidelines and the recommendations of experts."}, "https://uottawa.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/uOttawa_External_Career_Site/job/Ottawa-ON/APTPUO---Hiver-2027---PED3543-A100---VAL-APPRENTIS--L-LMENT_JR39293": {"title": "APTPUO - Hiver 2027 - PED3543 A100 - \u00c9VAL. APPRENTIS. \u00c0 L'\u00c9L\u00c9MENT.", "description": "Posted: 2026-09-23\nPart time\n\nPosting Reason: New Position Location: Main Campus Academic Period: 2027 Winter Semester Faculty: Facult\u00e9 d'\u00e9ducation / Faculty of Education Academic Unit: Formation \u00e0 l\u2019enseignement (Fac. Education) Course Title: \u00c9valuation des apprentissages \u00e0 l'\u00e9l\u00e9mentaire Course Code: PED 3543 Section: A100 Course Description: PED3543: \u00c9valuation des apprentissages \u00e0 l'\u00e9l\u00e9mentaire \u00c9tude des diff\u00e9rentes \u00e9tapes de l'\u00e9valuation scolaire. D\u00e9veloppement et analyse d'outils d'\u00e9valuation. \u00c9tude des contenus en lien avec les politiques du Minist\u00e8re de l'\u00c9ducation de l'Ontario. D\u00e9veloppement du jugement en \u00e9valuation des apprentissages. \u00c9tude de la nature, des fonctions et des finalit\u00e9s de l'\u00e9valuation. Veuillez noter que le cours est offert en personne Posting limited to: Professeur \u00e0 temps-partiel r\u00e9gulier / Regular Part-Time Professor Date