rts."}, "https://uottawa.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/uOttawa_External_Career_Site/job/Ottawa-ON/APTPUO---Winter-2027---ESL-2181-E00-for-ECO-1102_JR39515": {"title": "APTPUO - Winter 2027 - ESL 2181 E00 for ECO 1102", "description": "Posted: 2026-10-01\nPart time\n\nPosting Reason: New Position Location: Main Campus Academic Period: 2027 Winter Semester Faculty: Facult\u00e9 des arts / Faculty of Arts Academic Unit: Institut des langues officielles et du bilinguisme \\\\ Official Languages and Bilingualism Institute (OLBI) Course Title: Adjunct Language Course in ESL: Receptive Skills. Associated with ECO 1104 B00 Course Code: ESL 2181 Section: E00 Course Description: Adjunct english as a second language course to a 3-unit discipline-specific course (ECO 1102), taken in English by non-native speakers of English. Emphasis on development of comprehension skills (listening and reading) while acquiring knowledge and expertise in the discipline. Examination questions in the discipline-specific course may be answered in either English or French; however, all tests and assignments in the language class must be done in English. It is required that the ESL Professor attend the following discipline-specific course in addition to the language course: ECO 1102 D00 Tuesday 4:00pm-5:20pm and Thursday 2:30pm-3:50pm - in person Note: Students may be enrolled in sections D00, E00, F00 and G00 of the ECO 1102 course. Posting limited to: Professeur \u00e0 temps-partiel r\u00e9gulier / Regular Part-Time Professor Date Posted (YYYY/MM/DD): 2026/10/01 Applications must be received BEFORE (YYYY/MM/DD): 2026/11/01 Expected Enrolment: 30 Approval date: 2026/10/01 Number of credits: 3 Work Hours: 57 Hourly Rate: Cours de langue / Language Course: $203.54 (2024-2025) The academic year starts on September 1 and ends on August 31. These rates do not included vacation pay nor statutory pay. These rates will be applied until a new collective agreement is ratified. Retro will be paid after the ratificati