31 (Sept. 2026 - Aug. 2027) Undergraduate students will be paid at the lower rate; while graduate students will be paid at the higher rate. These rates do not include vacation pay nor statutory pay. Method of Delivery: In person Language of Work: Anglais | English Requirements and Nature of Work: Nature of Work The TA will assist in the delivery of C HM 2354 \u2013 Analytical Chemistry by leading DGD to support student learning. Responsibilities include: Preparing and facilitating DGD sessions (developing discussion outlines, examples, and exercises). Demonstrating problem-solving methods and responding to student questions. Reading and replying to student emails. Marking midterm and final examinations and entering grades. Assisting with midterm and final examination invigilation as assigned by the Faculty of Science. Attending course team meetings and performing related clerical or administrative tasks (e.g., preparing materials, photocopying, organizing exams). Minimum Qualifications Completion of one full year of general chemistry and CHM 2354 Analytical Chemistry or an equivalent course. Candidates who are not Chemistry graduate students will be required to complete a qualifying test (unless previously completed). Successful completion of WHMIS and Occupational Health and Safety training prior to appointment. Required Skills Strong knowledge of analytical chemistry concepts and quantitative problem-solving techniques. Excellent communication and organizational skills. Ability to work both independently and collaboratively in an academic setting. Additional Information and/or Comments: All University of Ottawa employees are required under provincial law to successfully complete all mandatory legislated training offered by the University. The list of training requirements may be modified by provincial law. If you are invited to continue the selection process, please notify us of any particular adaptive measures you might require. We may consult with the Health and