terest in Conflict Studies and Human Rights; - Capacity to communicate clearly in English and French. - Teaching assistant, group facilitation and/or grading experience are an advantage. COURSE SCHEDULE: Wednesday 10 am to 11:20 am Friday 8:30 am to 9:50 am METHOD:\u00a0 IN PERSON Additional Information and/or Comments: All University of Ottawa employees are required under provincial law to successfully complete all mandatory legislated training offered by the University. The list of training requirements may be modified by provincial law. If you are invited to continue the selection process, please notify us of any particular adaptive measures you might require. We may consult with the Health and Wellness sector of Human Resources, if needed. Any information you send us will be handled respectfully and in complete confidence. The hiring process will be governed by the current CUPE 2626 collective agreement; you can click here to find out more. The University of Ottawa embraces diversity and inclusion in the workplace. We are passionate about our people and committed to employment equity. We foster a culture of respect, teamwork and inclusion, where collaboration, innovation, and creativity fuel our quest for research and teaching excellence. While all qualified persons are invited to apply, we welcome applications from qualified Indigenous persons, racialized persons, persons with disabilities, women and LGBTQIA2S+ persons. The University is committed to creating and maintaining an accessible, barrier-free work environment. The University is also committed to working with applicants with disabilities requesting accommodation during the recruitment, assessment and selection processes. Applicants with disabilities may contact the academic unit to communicate the accommodation need. Prior to May 1, 2022, the University required all students, faculty, staff, and visitors (including contractors) to be fully vaccinated against Covid-19 as defined in Policy 129 \u2013 Covid-19 Vaccination. This policy was suspended effective May 1, 2022 but may be reinstated at any point in the future depending on public health guidelines and the recommendations of experts."}, "https://uottawa.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/uOttawa_External_Career_Site/job/Ottawa-ON/Assistanat-de-recherche--Dpartement-de-franais---Automne-2026---Hiver-2027_JR40582-1": {"title": "Assistanat de recherche -D\u00e9partement de fran\u00e7ais - Automne 2026 - Hiver 2027", "description": "Posted: 2026-10-26\nPart time\n\nPosting Reason: New Position Location where work is to be performed: Main Campus Session: 2026 Fall Semester | Trimestre d'automne Faculty: Facult\u00e9 des arts / Faculty of Arts Unit: D\u00e9partement de fran\u00e7ais_Students and Casuals Job Classification: Research Assistant (CUPE) Posting Type: Recherche / Research Course Title: N/A Course Code: N/A Section: Supervisor name (if known): Kasereka Kavwahirehi Date Posted (YYYY/MM/DD): 2026/10/26 Applications must be received BEFORE (YYYY/MM/DD): 2026/11/08 Description of tasks (hours): Unless specified below, specific allocation of hours to various tasks should be articulated in a description of work negotiated and signed by you and the supervising professor prior to the commencement of work. Recherche / Research:0 Pr\u00e9paration / Preparation:0 Contact avec \u00e9tudiants / Contact with Students:0 Correction - Notation / Grading:0 Surveillance / Proctoring:0 Formation / Training:0 Autre / Other:0 Number of positions: 1 Expected Enrolment: N/A Work Start Date: October 26, 2026 Work End Date: January 31, 2027 Total Work Hours: 60 Hourly Rate: AE-RA-Tuteur / TA-RA-Tutor : $33.83 ou/or $53.31 (Sept. 2026 - Aug. 2027) Undergraduate students will be paid at the lower rate; while graduate students will be paid at the higher rate. These rates do not include vacation pay nor statutory pay. Method of Delivery: In person Language of Work: Fran\u00e7ais | French Requirements and Nature of Work: Exigences minimales : Ma\u00eetrise en lettres fran\u00e7aises ou dans un domaine \u00e9quivalent. Excellente ma\u00eetrise du fran\u00e7ais \u00e9crit. Avoir compl\u00e9t\u00e9 les formations requises par l\u2019Universit\u00e9 pour l\u2019acc\u00e8s aux sites Internet ou avoir la disponibilit\u00e9 pour les suivre \u00e0 courte \u00e9ch\u00e9ance. Exp\u00e9rience pr\u00e9alable dans la r\u00e9daction de communications professionnelles, ainsi qu\u2019en cr\u00e9ation de contenu et en gestion de r\u00e9seaux sociaux. \u00a0 Description de l\u2019emploi L\u2019assistant ou l\u2019assistante de recherche aura pour t\u00e2che principale de contribuer aux travaux de recherche en effectuant des recherches bibliographiques et en assurant la synth\u00e8se de la documentation pertinente au projet. \u00a0 T\u00e2ches principales : Effectuer des recherches bibliographiques afin de rep\u00e9rer des articles et des publications pertinents au projet de recherche. Lire les articles et les documents scientifiques s\u00e9lectionn\u00e9s. R\u00e9diger des r\u00e9sum\u00e9s des articles consult\u00e9s en faisant ressortir les id\u00e9es principales et les \u00e9l\u00e9ments pertinents pour le projet. Organiser et classer la documentation recueillie afin de faciliter sa consultation. Contribuer \u00e0 la pr\u00e9paration et \u00e0 la synth\u00e8se de la documentation n\u00e9cessaire aux travaux de recherche. \u00a0\u00a0 Additional Information and/or Comments: All University of Ottawa employees are required under provincial law to successfully complete all mandatory legislated training offered by the University. The list of training requirements may be modified by provincial law. If you are invited to continue the selection process, please notify us of any particular adaptive measures you might require. We may consult with the Health and Wellness sector of Human Resources, if needed. Any information you send us will be handled respectfully and in complete confidence. The hiring process will be governed by the current CUPE 2626 collective agreement; you can click here to find out more. The University of Ottawa embraces diversity and inclusion in the workplace. We are passionate about our people and committed to employment equity. We foster a culture of respect, teamwork and inclusion, where collaboration, innovation, and creativity fuel our quest for research and teaching excellence. While all qualified persons are invited to apply, we welcome applications from qualified Indigenous persons, racialized persons, persons with disabilities, women and LGBTQIA2S+ persons. The University is committed to creating and maintaining an accessible, barrier-free work environment. The University is also committed to working with applicants with disabilities requesting accommodation during the recruitment, assessment and selection processes. Applicants with disabilities may contact the academic unit to communicate the accommodation need. Prior to May 1, 2022, the University required all students, faculty, staff, and visitors (including contractors) to be fully vaccinated against Covid-19 as defined in Policy 129 \u2013 Covid-19 Vaccination. This policy was suspended effective May 1, 2022 but may be reinstated at any point in the future depending on public health guidelines and the recommendations of experts."}, "https://uottawa.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/uOttawa_External_Career_Site/job/Ottawa-ON/CUPE---Winter-2027---ECH-2330A--TA-_JR40375": {"title": "CUPE - Winter 2027 - ECH 2330A (TA)", "description": "Posted: 2026-10-26\nPart time\n\nPosting Reason: New Position Location where work is to be performed: Main Campus Session: 2027 Winter Semester | Trimestre d'hiver Faculty: Facult\u00e9 des sciences sociales / Faculty of Social Sciences Unit: Graduate School of Public and International Affairs_ST Job Classification: Teaching Assistant/Demonstrator/Lab Monitor (CUPE) Posting Type: Cours pr\u00e9cis / Specific course Course Title: Theories of Conflict Course Code: ECH 2330 Section: A Supervisor