uary 01, 2027 Work End Date: April 30, 2027 Total Work Hours: 130 Hourly Rate: AE-RA-Tuteur / TA-RA-Tutor : $33.83 ou/or $53.31 (Sept. 2026 - Aug. 2027) Undergraduate students will be paid at the lower rate; while graduate students will be paid at the higher rate. These rates do not include vacation pay nor statutory pay. Method of Delivery: IN PERSON Language of Work: Anglais | English Requirements and Nature of Work: Nature of Work: Correcting assignments and lab reports, supervising labs, directing group projects, providing office hours, assisting in preparing labs, project descriptions and sample programs. \u00a0Correcting midterm. Proctoring. Minimum Requirements: Preference will be given to candidates who have \u00a0completed CEG4166 (or equivalent such as CSI4141 or SEG4145) with a minimum of A. \u00a0Attend a TA workshop if necessary. Must be ready for an interview if considered for this position. The responsibilities include TUT and LAB supervision, the applicant must be available for both of these. In-depth knowledge and experience with C programming. \u00a0Knowledge and experienced with embedded systems. Knowledge and experience with agile software development methods (in particular SCRUM) would be an asset. Crosslisted: CEG4166/CSI4141/SEG4145. Please note that the teaching method will be delivered: in person. \u200bNOTE: le nombre de postes et le nombre d'heures offertes sont tous deux assujettis aux inscriptions finales dans ce cours. Please note that the number of hours and positions offered may vary due to enrolments in that course. Additional Information and/or Comments: All University of Ottawa employees are required under provincial law to successfully complete all mandatory legislated training offered by the University. The list of training requirements may be modified by provincial law. If you are invited to continue the selection process, please notify us of any particular adaptive measures you might require. We may consult with the Health and 