itle": "APTPUO - Hiver 2027 - PED4600 P01 - STAGE II MILIEU SCOL. \u00c9L\u00c9MENT.", "description": "Posted: 2026-10-21\nPart time\n\nPosting Reason: New Position Location: Main Campus Academic Period: 2027 Winter Semester Faculty: Facult\u00e9 d'\u00e9ducation / Faculty of Education Academic Unit: Formation \u00e0 l\u2019enseignement (Fac. Education) Course Title: Stage II en milieu scolaire \u00e9l\u00e9mentaire Course Code: PED4600 Section: P01 Course Description: Gestion, prise en charge et analyse de l'enseignement aux cycles primaire et moyen. Approfondissement des diff\u00e9rents aspects de la profession enseignante. Retour r\u00e9flexif sur les notions th\u00e9oriques et sur les exp\u00e9riences r\u00e9alis\u00e9es dans le cadre des stages et des s\u00e9minaires d'int\u00e9gration. \u00c9laboration d'un dossier professionnel d'apprentissage. Le stage a lieu du 04 janvier au 23 avril 2027. Mode d'enseignement: Cours hybride en pr\u00e9sentiel, alternant pr\u00e9sentiel et distance Posting limited to: Professeur \u00e0 temps-partiel r\u00e9gulier / Regular Part-Time Professor Date Posted (YYYY/MM/DD): 2026/10/21 Applications must be received BEFORE (YYYY/MM/DD): 2026/11/22 Expected Enrolment: 20 Approval date: 2026/10/21 Number of credits: 3 Work Hours: 39 Hourly Rate: Enseignement / Teaching: $239.47 (2024-2025) The academic year starts on September 1 and ends on August 31. These rates do not included vacation pay nor statutory pay. These rates will be applied until a new collective agreement is ratified. Retro will be paid after the ratification. Course type: D Posting type: R\u00e9gulier / Regular Language of instruction: Fran\u00e7ais | French Competence in second language: Passive Course Schedule: Jeudi | Thursday 17:30-20:30 Jeudi | Thursday 17:30-20:30 Vendredi | Friday - Cours offer en mode hybride en pr\u00e9sentiel Requirements: Objectif du poste: Le programme de formation \u00e0 l\u2019enseignement de la Facult\u00e9 d\u2019\u00e9ducation de l\u2019Universit\u00e9 d\u2019Ottawa recrute des professeures conseill\u00e8res et de professeurs conseillers pour accompagner des stagiaires en enseignement aux cycles primaire, moyen, interm\u00e9diaire et sup\u00e9rieur. Ce r\u00f4le s\u2019inscrit dans une d\u00e9marche de formation pratique visant \u00e0 soutenir le d\u00e9veloppement professionnel des futurs enseignants. Responsabilit\u00e9s principales du poste: La professeure conseill\u00e8re ou le professeur conseiller aura pour mission, entre autres, de : \u2756 Offrir un accompagnement p\u00e9dagogique et un soutien affectif favorisant le d\u00e9veloppement progressif des comp\u00e9tences professionnelles en enseignement, \u00e0 travers des r\u00e9troactions constructives, cibl\u00e9es et adapt\u00e9es au niveau du stagiaire ; \u2756 Mettre en place des modalit\u00e9s efficaces de supervision \u00e0 distance, en utilisant des outils num\u00e9riques appropri\u00e9s et en veillant au respect des principes li\u00e9s \u00e0 l\u2019\u00e9thique et \u00e0 la confidentialit\u00e9; \u2756 Soutenir activement l\u2019enseignante accompagnatrice ou l\u2019enseignant accompagnateur afin d\u2019assurer une coh\u00e9rence et une compl\u00e9mentarit\u00e9 dans l\u2019encadrement du stagiaire ; \u2756 Planifier, r\u00e9aliser et documenter des s\u00e9ances d\u2019observation, ainsi que des rencontres de r\u00e9troaction en dyade et en triade \u00e0 distance, en s\u2019appuyant sur des outils num\u00e9riques facilitant l\u2019analyse r\u00e9flexive ; \u2756 Participer \u00e0 la s\u00e9ance d\u2019information obligatoire le 7 janvier 2027 (10 h \u00e0 12 h) . \u2756 Animer les s\u00e9minaires de stage aux dates suivantes : Jeudi 14 janvier 2027 - 17h30 \u00e0 20h20 (Mode AU) Jeudi 18 f\u00e9vrier 2027 - 17h30 \u00e0 20h20 (Mode AU) Vendredi 23 avril 2027 - 17h30 \u00e0 20h20 (En Pr\u00e9sentiel) \u2756 Attribuer la note sommative du stage et entrer la note sommative du stage dans le registre pr\u00e9vu \u00e0 cet effet au plus tard dans les 10 jours suivant la fin du stage. Qualifications minimales requises pour le poste: - Ma\u00eetrise en \u00e9ducation. - Qualification dans un domaine li\u00e9 \u00e0 l'enseignement dans les \u00e9coles de langue fran\u00e7aise en Ontario. - Exp\u00e9rience r\u00e9cente dans l'enseignement ou l'administration scolaire au niveau primaire/junior/\u00e9l\u00e9mentaire. - Connaissance du programme d'\u00e9tudes de l'Ontario, des normes de pratique de la profession enseignante et du code de d\u00e9ontologie de l'Ordre des enseignantes et des enseignants de l'Ontario. - L'universit\u00e9 peut prendre en consid\u00e9ration une exp\u00e9rience ou des qualifications \u00e9quivalentes \u00e0 celles mentionn\u00e9es ci-dessus. Un niveau d'\u00e9ducation/d'exp\u00e9rience jug\u00e9 \u00e9quivalentes pourrait suppl\u00e9er aux exigences d'\u00e9ducation et/ou d'exp\u00e9rience requises. Si on vous invite \u00e0 poursuivre les \u00e9tapes du processus de s\u00e9lection, veuillez nous aviser de tout besoin n\u00e9cessitant des mesures d'adaptation. Les renseignements communiqu\u00e9s seront trait\u00e9s avec respect et confidentialit\u00e9. Les employ\u00e9(e)s sont tenus(e) par la loi provinciale de mener \u00e0 bien des formations obligatoires. La liste des formations peut \u00eatre modifi\u00e9e par une loi provincial. Additional Information and/or Comments: An acceptable level of education and/or experience could be viewed as being equivalent to the educational required and/or demonstrated experience. If you are invited to continue the selection process, please notify us of any adaptive measures you might require. Information you send us will be handled respectfully and in complete confidence. Employees are required under provincial law to successfully complete all mandatory legislated training. The list of training may be modified by provincial law. The hiring process will be governed by the current APTPUO collective agreements; you can click here for the main unit , here for the OLBI unit , or here for the Toronto/Windsor unit to find out more. The University of Ottawa embraces diversity and inclusion in the workplace. We are passionate about our people and committed to employment equity. We foster a culture of respect, teamwork and inclusion, where collaboration, innovation, and creativity fuel our quest for research and teaching excellence. While all qualified persons are invited to apply, we welcome applications from qualified Indigenous persons, racialized persons, persons with disabilities, women and LGBTQIA2S+ persons. The University is committed to creating and maintaining an accessible, barrier-free work environment. The University is also committed to working with applicants with disabilities requesting accommodation during the recruitment, assessment and selection processes. Applicants with disabilities may contact vra.affairesprofessorales@uottawa.ca to communicate the accommodation need. All qualified candidates are encouraged to apply; however, Canadians and permanent residents will be given priority. Prior to May 1, 2022, the University required all students, faculty, staff, and visitors (including contractors) to be fully vaccinated against Covid-19 as defined in Policy 129 \u2013 Covid-19 Vaccination. This policy was suspended effective May 1, 2022 but may be reinstated at any point in the future depending on public health guidelines and the recommendations of experts."}, "https://uottawa.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/uOttawa_External_Career_Site/job/Ottawa-ON/Cupe--Automne-2026---Correcteur-d-examens---M-Giroux_JR40351": {"title": "Cupe -Automne 2026 - Correcteur d'examens - M. Giroux", "description": "Posted: 2026-10-20\nPart time\n\nPosting Reason: New Position Location where work is to be performed: Main Campus Session: 2026 Fall Semester | Trimestre d'automne Faculty: Section de droit civil / Civil Law Section Unit: Michelle Giroux_Students Job Classification: Corrector (CUPE) Posting Type: Cours pr\u00e9cis / Specific course Course Title: Personne et famille Course Code: DRC1506 C / 4792 C Section: Supervisor name (if known): Date Posted (YYYY/MM/DD): 2026/10/20 Applications must be received BEFORE (YYYY/MM/DD): 2026/10/29 Description of tasks (hours): Unless specified below, specific allocation of hours to various tasks should be articulated in a description of work negotiated and signed by you and the supervising professor prior to the commencement of work. Recherche / Research:0 Pr\u00e9paration / Preparation:0 Contact avec \u00e9tudiants / Contact with Students:0 Correction - Notation / Grading:0 Surveillance / Proctoring:0 Formation / Training:0 Autre / Other:0 Number of positions: 1 Expected Enrolment: n/a Work Start Date: December 15, 2026 Work End Date: January 07, 2027 Total Work Hours: 73.5 Hourly Rate: Correcteur / Corrector : $31.44 ou/or $37.73 (Sept. 2025 - Aug. 2026) Undergraduate students will be paid at the lower rate; while graduate students will be paid at the higher rate. These rates do not include vacation pay nor statutory pay. Method of Delivery: n/a Language of Work: Anglais | English, Fran\u00e7ais | French Requirements and Nature of Work: Assistanat de correction pour le cours DRC1506 C / 4792 C \u00a0Personne et famille . \u00a0 Avoir un int\u00e9r\u00eat pour la mati\u00e8re vis\u00e9e par le cours (sur pr\u00e9sentation d\u2019une lettre de motivation et/ou d\u2019un c.v.); Avoir suivi et r\u00e9ussi le cours en question avec de bons r\u00e9sultats (sur pr\u00e9sentation d\u2019un relev\u00e9 de notes); Sens du d\u00e9tail, rigueur, jugement, autonomie; Bon sens de l\u2019organisation; Respect des d\u00e9lais; Excellente ma\u00eetrise du fran\u00e7ais; bonne connaissance de l'anglais Une exp\u00e9rience dans le cadre d\u2019un assistanat de correction ou de recherche dans cette mati\u00e8re est un atout. Dates vis\u00e9es\u00a0: l\u2019examen aura lieu le 18 d\u00e9cembre et la correction doit \u00eatre effectu\u00e9e entre le19 d\u00e9cembre et 7 janvier. Additional Information and/or Comments: All University of Ottawa employees are required under provincial law to successfully complete all mandatory legislated training offered by the University. The list of training requirements may be modified by provincial law. If you are invited to continue the selection process, please notify us of any particular adaptive measures you might require. We may consult with the Health and Wellness sector of Human Resources, if needed. Any information you send us will be handled respectfully and in complete confidence. The hiring process will be governed by the current CUPE 2626 collective agreement; you can click here to find out more. The University of Ottawa embraces diversity and inclusion in the workplace. We are passionate about our people and committed to employment equity. We foster a culture of respect, teamwork and inclusion, where collaboration, innovation, and creativity fuel our quest for research and teaching excellence. While all qualified persons are invited to apply, we welcome applications from qualified Indigenous persons, racialized persons, persons with disabilities, women and LGBTQIA2S+ persons. The University is committed to creating and maintaining an accessible, barrier-free work environment. The University is also committed to working with applicants with disabilities requesting accommodation during the recruitment, assessment and selection processes. Applicants with disabilities may contact the academic unit to communicate the accommodation need. Prior to May 1, 2022, the University required all students, faculty, staff, and visitors (including contractors) to be fully vaccinated against Covid-19 as defined in Policy 129 \u2013 Covid-19 Vaccination. This policy was suspended effective May 1, 2022 but may be reinstated at any point in the future depending on public health guidelines and the recommendations of experts."}, "https://uottawa.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/uOttawa_External_Career_Site/job/Ottawa-ON/Cupe--Automne-2026---Correcteur-d-examens---D-Robitaille_JR40349": {"title": "Cupe -Automne 2026 - Correcteur d'examens - D. Robitaille", "description": "Posted: 2026-10-20\nPart time\n\nPosting Reason: New Position Location where work is to be performed: Main Campus Session: 2026 Fall Semester | Trimestre d'automne Faculty: Section de droit civil / Civil Law Section Unit: David Robitaille_Students Job Classification: Corrector (CUPE) Posting Type: Recherche / Research Course Title: Droits et libert\u00e9s - Droit des collectivit\u00e9s locales Course Code: DRC 2509 A - DRC 2509 A Section: Supervisor name (if known): Date Posted (YYYY/MM/DD): 2026/10/20 Applications must be received BEFORE (YYYY/MM/DD): 2026/10/29 Description of tasks (hours): Unless specified below, specific allocation of hours to various tasks should be articulated in a description of work negotiated and signed by you and the supervising professor prior to the commencement of work. Recherche / Research:0 Pr\u00e9paration / Preparation:0 Contact avec \u00e9tudiants / Contact with Students:0 Correction - Notation / Grading:0 Surveillance / Proctoring:0 Formation / Training:0 Autre / Other:0 Number of positions: 1 Expected Enrolment: n/a Work Start Date: November 02, 2026 Work End Date: December 31, 2026 Total Work Hours: 55.5 Hourly Rate: Correcteur / Corrector : $32.39 ou/or $38.86 (Sept. 2026 - Aug. 2027) Undergraduate students will be paid at the lower rate; while graduate students will be paid at the higher rate. These rates do not include vacation pay nor statutory pay. Method of Delivery: n/a Language of Work: Anglais | English, Fran\u00e7ais | French Requirements and Nature of Work: Les exigences requises pour le poste : \u00b7\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0 Avoir un int\u00e9r\u00eat pour la mati\u00e8re vis\u00e9e par le cours (sur pr\u00e9sentation d\u2019une lettre de motivation et/ou d\u2019un c.v.); \u00b7\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0 Avoir suivi et r\u00e9ussi le cours avec de tr\u00e8s bons r\u00e9sultats (sur pr\u00e9sentation d\u2019un relev\u00e9 de notes); \u00b7\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0 Sens du d\u00e9tail, rigueur, jugement, autonomie; \u00b7\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0 Bon sens de l\u2019organisation; \u00b7\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0 Respect des d\u00e9lais; \u00b7\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0 Excellente ma\u00eetrise du fran\u00e7ais et de l'anglais; \u00b7\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0 Une exp\u00e9rience en correction ou en recherche dans cette mati\u00e8re est un atout. Additional Information and/or Comments: All University of Ottawa employees are required under provincial law to successfully complete all mandatory legislated training offered by the University. The list of training requirements may be modified by provincial law. If you are invited to continue the selection process, please notify us of any particular adaptive measures you might require. We may consult with the Health and Wellness sector of Human Resources, if needed. Any information you send us will be handled respectfully and in complete confidence. The hiring process will be governed by the current CUPE 2626 collective agreement; you can click here to find out more. The University of Ottawa embraces diversity and inclusion in the workplace. We are passionate about our people and committed to employment equity. We foster a culture of respect, teamwork and inclusion, where collaboration, innovation, and creativity fuel our quest for research and teaching excellence. While all qualified persons are invited to apply, we welcome applications from qualified Indigenous persons, racialized persons, persons with disabilities, women and LGBTQIA2S+ persons. The University is committed to creating and maintaining an accessible, barrier-free work environment. The University is also committed to working with applicants with disabilities requesting accommodation during the recruitment, assessment and selection processes. Applicants with disabilities may contact the academic unit to communicate the accommodation need. Prior to May 1, 2022, the University required all students, faculty, staff, and visitors (including contractors) to be fully vaccinated against Covid-19 as defined in Policy 129 \u2013 Covid-19 Vaccination. This policy was suspended effective May 1, 2022 but may be reinstated at any point in the future depending on public health guidelines and the recommendations of experts."}, "https://uottawa.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/uOttawa_External_Career_Site/job/Ottawa-ON/Veterinarian_JR40345": {"title": "Veterinarian", "description": "Posted: 2026-10-20\nFull time\n\nFollow us on LinkedIn Posting Reason: Replacement of a regular position Job Type: Employee Anticipated Duration in Months (for contracts and temporary assignments): N/A Job Family: Laboratory Support # of Open Positions: 1 Faculty/Service - Department: Animal Care and Veterinary Services Campus: Smyth, Alta Vista, General Hospital, CHEO Campuses Union Affiliation: N/A Date Posted (YYYY/MM/DD): 2026/10/20 Applications must be received BEFORE (YYYY/MM/DD): Hours per week: 35 Salary Grade: Non-Union Grade NM2 Salary Range: $118,675.00 - $148,344.00 Additional compensation may be available based on the specific requirements of the position and applicable University compensation practices. Details regarding the complete compensation package will be discussed with qualified candidates during the recruitment process. Position Purpose The Clinical Veterinarian provides advanced veterinary medical care and clinical oversight in support of the University's animal care, teaching, and research programs. As a key subject matter expert within Animal Care and Veterinary Services, the incumbent collaborates closely with researchers, veterinary technicians, animal care personnel, and other stakeholders to promote animal health and welfare, support the ethical and effective use of animals in research and teaching, and ensure the delivery of high-quality veterinary services. The role is responsible for providing clinical, diagnostic, medical, and surgical care to a diverse range of animal species, while overseeing preventive medicine and health surveillance programs. The Clinical Veterinarian provides veterinary consultation and research support, including guidance on the development and use of appropriate animal models, review of animal use protocols, and participation in pre-, intra-, and post-operative procedures. The incumbent also develops and maintains site- and study-specific standard operating procedures and contributes to the continuous improvement of veterinary and animal care practices. Working in partnership with the Senior Director, Animal Care and Veterinary Services, the Clinical Veterinarian supports the implementation, delivery, and ongoing oversight of the University's veterinary care program. In this role, your responsibilities will include: Clinical Veterinary Care Provide preventive, diagnostic, medical, and surgical care for a diverse range of research animal species. Assess, diagnose, and manage clinical cases, including complex medical and surgical conditions. Develop and oversee treatment, monitoring, and recovery plans. Provide emergency and after-hours veterinary support as required. Perform clinical examinations, surgical procedures, and specialized veterinary interventions. Research Support and Consultation Provide veterinary consultation to researchers during study planning, protocol development, and study execution. Advise on anesthesia, analgesia, perioperative care, animal models, and humane endpoints. Support the development and refinement of research procedures to promote animal welfare and scientific integrity. Collaborate with investigators to address animal health concerns that may impact research outcomes. Animal Welfare and Clinical Oversight Monitor animal health and welfare across research colonies and studies. Assess and manage animal welfare concerns and implement appropriate interventions. Recommend modifications to procedures or care plans based on veterinary assessment. Contribute to post-approval monitoring and veterinary review activities. Education and Training Provide clinical guidance to veterinary technicians, animal care personnel, students, and researchers. Participate in the development and delivery of training programs related to animal health, surgery, anesthesia, and animal welfare. Mentor veterinary and technical staff in clinical techniques and best practices. Program Development and Quality Improvement Contribute to the continuous improvement of veterinary and animal care programs. Develop and maintain clinical protocols, standards, and operating procedures. Participate in quality assurance initiatives, adverse event reviews, and program evaluations. Maintain comprehensive and accurate medical records and clinical documentation. What you will bring: Doctor of Veterinary Medicine (DVM) or equivalent veterinary degree\u00a0 Active license with the College of Veterinarians of Ontario (CVO) to practice veterinary medicine in Ontario\u00a0 A minimum of three (3) years of experience in laboratory animal medicine, or equivalent specialized training and clinical experience, including: completion of a recognized residency in laboratory animal medicine; or demonstrated substantial clinical rotations, internships, externships or other structured training in laboratory animal medicine as part of a DVM program or post-graduate training. A minimum of two (2) years of experience supervising or managing personnel is an asset. Demonstrated knowledge and clinical experience in laboratory animal medicine, including laboratory animal diseases and pathology, animal model development, anesthesia and analgesia, perioperative care, and surgical procedures. The incumbent must have strong initiative and be able to resolve challenges on his/her own, in addition to being an excellent team player.\u00a0\u00a0 Experience with large and small animal models desirable Experience in the care of aquatic and reptile species desirable The incumbent should be conversant with surgical procedures as defined in approved animal use protocols Excellent interpersonal and communications skills as well as a service-oriented approach are essential. The position requires an ongoing interface with Principal Investigators and their laboratory staff.\u00a0 The applicant must be very knowledgeable with regard to the Animals for Research Act as well as the guidelines and policies of the Canadian Council on Animal Care Ability to work after hours on weekends and statutory holidays and to be on a rotating on-call schedule for evenings, weekends and holiday coverage. Bilingualism \u2013 French and English (spoken and written). Key Competencies at uOttawa: Here are the required competencies for all or our employees at uOttawa:\u00a0 Planning: Organize in time a series of actions or events in order to realize an objective or a project. Plan and organize own work and priorities in regular daily activities. Initiative: Demonstrate creativity and initiative to suggest improvements and encourage positive results. Is proactive and self-starting. Show availability and willingness to go above and beyond whenever it is possible. Client Service Orientation: Help or serve others to meet their needs. This implies anticipating and identifying the needs of internal and external clients and finding solutions on how to meet them. Teamwork and Cooperation: Cooperate and work well with other members of the team to reach common goal(s). Accept and give constructive feedback. Able to adjust own behaviour to reach the goals of the team. The University of Ottawa embraces diversity and inclusion in the workplace. We are passionate about our people and committed to employment equity. We foster a culture of respect, teamwork and inclusion, where collaboration, innovation, and creativity fuel our quest for research and teaching excellence. While all qualified persons are invited to apply, we welcome applications from qualified Indigenous persons, racialized persons, persons with disabilities, women and LGBTQIA2S+ persons. The University is committed to creating and maintaining an accessible, barrier-free work environment. The University is also committed to working with applicants with disabilities requesting accommodation during the recruitment, assessment and selection processes. Applicants with disabilities may contact hrtalentmanagement@uottawa.ca to communicate the accommodation need. All qualified candidates are encouraged to apply; however, Canadians and permanent residents will be given priority. Note: if this is a union position: The hiring process will be governed by the current collective agreement related to the union affiliation noted above; you can click here to find out more. If this is a front-line position with responsibilities to interact with students, selected candidates must be rated at the Low Advanced proficiency level or higher for both oral comprehension and reading comprehension in their second official language. The rating is determined by a proficiency test designed by the Official Languages and Bilingualism Institute. Prior to May 1, 2022, the University required all students, faculty, staff, and visitors (including contractors) to be fully vaccinated against Covid-19 as defined in Policy 129 \u2013 Covid-19 Vaccination. This policy was suspended effective May 1, 2022 but may be reinstated at any point in the future depending on public health guidelines and the recommendations of experts."}, "https://uottawa.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/uOttawa_External_Career_Site/job/Main-Campus/ATPUO---Winter-2027---ADM2304M---Applications-of-Statistical-Methods-in-Business_JR40343": {"title": "ATPUO - Winter 2027 - ADM2304M - Applications of Statistical Methods in Business", "description": "Posted: 2026-10-20\nPart time\n\nPosting Reason: New Position Location: Ottawa, ON Academic Period: 2027 Winter Semester Faculty: \u00c9cole de gestion Telfer / Telfer School of Management Academic Unit: Telfer School of Management Course Title: Applications of Statistical Methods in Business Course Code: ADM2304 Section: M Course Description: Topics include the estimation (using confidence intervals) and hypothesis testing (including non-parametric methods); correlation and the simple linear regression model (with extensions to multiple regression); and chi-square tests on qualitative data. Emphasis on understanding when and how to use (and not misuse) various methods. Hands-on experience with statistical software tools. (The lab is optional.) Posting limited to: Professeur \u00e0 temps-partiel \u00e9tudiant\u00a0/ Student Part-Time Professor Date Posted (YYYY/MM/DD): 2026/10/20 Applications must be received BEFORE (YYYY/MM/DD): 2026/11/21 Expected Enrolment: 90 Approval date: 2026/10/20 Number of credits: 3 Work Hours: 39 Hourly Rate: Enseignement / Teaching: $239.47 (2024-2025) The academic year starts on September 1 and ends on August 31. These rates do not included vacation pay nor statutory pay. These rates will be applied until a new collective agreement is ratified. Retro will be paid after the ratification. Course type: C Posting type: R\u00e9gulier / Regular Language of instruction: Anglais | English Competence in second language: Passive Course Schedule: Lundi | Monday 14:30-16:00 Jeudi | Thursday 16:00-17:30 - Requirements: Must have a Master's degree (PhD preferred) in statistics or in a field of study where statistical methods were applied extensively. Must also demonstrate recent professional experience directly related to the use of statistical methods in business. Must also have teaching experience, preferably in the area of the course. Teaching mode: Please note that the teaching method will be delivered in person. Teaching method might incur changes due to health measures or other reasons. Additional Information and/or Comments: An acceptable level of education and/or experience could be viewed as being equivalent to the educational required and/or demonstrated experience. If you are invited to continue the selection process, please notify us of any adaptive measures you might require. Information you send us will be handled respectfully and in complete confidence. Employees are required under provincial law to successfully complete all mandatory legislated training. The list of training may be modified by provincial law. The hiring process will be governed by the current APTPUO collective agreements; you can click here for the main unit , here for the OLBI unit , or here for the Toronto/Windsor unit to find out more. The University of Ottawa embraces diversity and inclusion in the workplace. We are passionate about our people and committed to employment equity. We foster a culture of respect, teamwork and inclusion, where collaboration, innovation, and creativity fuel our quest for research and teaching excellence. While all qualified persons are invited to apply, we welcome applications from qualified Indigenous persons, racialized persons, persons with disabilities, women and LGBTQIA2S+ persons. The University is committed to creating and maintaining an accessible, barrier-free work environment. The University is also committed to working with applicants with disabilities requesting accommodation during the recruitment, assessment and selection processes. Applicants with disabilities may contact vra.affairesprofessorales@uottawa.ca to communicate the accommodation need. All qualified candidates are encouraged to apply; however, Canadians and permanent residents will be given priority. Prior to May 1, 2022, the University required all students, faculty, staff, and visitors (including contractors) to be fully vaccinated against Covid-19 as defined in Policy 129 \u2013 Covid-19 Vaccination. This policy was suspended effective May 1, 2022 but may be reinstated at any point in the future depending on public health guidelines and the recommendations of experts."}, "https://uottawa.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/uOttawa_External_Career_Site/job/Ottawa-ON/CUPE---Winter-2027---Research-Assistant---ALevesque---CML_JR40340": {"title": "CUPE - Winter 2027 - Research Assistant - A.Levesque - CML", "description": "Posted: 2026-10-20\nPart time\n\nPosting Reason: New Position Location where work is to be performed: Main Campus Session: 2027 Winter Semester | Trimestre d'hiver Faculty: Section de Common Law / Common Law Section Unit: Common Law_ST Job Classification: Research Assistant (CUPE) Posting Type: Recherche / Research Course Title: N/A Course Code: N/A Section: Supervisor name (if known): Date Posted (YYYY/MM/DD): 2026/10/20 Applications must be received BEFORE (YYYY/MM/DD): 2026/11/04 Description of tasks (hours): Unless specified below, specific allocation of hours to various tasks should be articulated in a description of work negotiated and signed by you and the supervising professor prior to the commencement of work. Recherche / Research:0 Pr\u00e9paration / Preparation:0 Contact avec \u00e9tudiants / Contact with Students:0 Correction - Notation / Grading:0 Surveillance / Proctoring:0 Formation / Training:0 Autre / Other:0 Number of positions: 1 Expected Enrolment: N/A Work Start Date: janvier 04, 2027 Work End Date: avril 30, 2027 Total Work Hours: 90 Hourly Rate: AE-RA-Tuteur / TA-RA-Tutor : $33.83 ou/or $53.31 (Sept. 2026 - Aug. 2027) Undergraduate students will be paid at the lower rate; while graduate students will be paid at the higher rate. These rates do not include vacation pay nor statutory pay. Method of Delivery: N/A Language of Work: Anglais | English, Fran\u00e7ais | French Requirements and Nature of Work: Nature of the work: Diverse research on social justice and human rights in Canada; assistance and support with drafting; footnotes; and administrative tasks. Minimum qualifications: Passionate about social justice and human rights. Resourcefulness. Experience in legal research, at the Equality Law Clinic, or in a social justice setting is a plus. Bilingual (French and English), both spoken and written. Excellent command of legal writing in both languages, with attention to detail and a thorough knowledge of common law terminology in French. This contract starts in November 2026. That said, to be considered for this position, you must also apply to job posting JR40336 for the fall 2026 semester. Additional Information and/or Comments: All University of Ottawa employees are required under provincial law to successfully complete all mandatory legislated training offered by the University. The list of training requirements may be modified by provincial law. If you are invited to continue the selection process, please notify us of any particular adaptive measures you might require. We may consult with the Health and Wellness sector of Human Resources, if needed. Any information you send us will be handled respectfully and in complete confidence. The hiring process will be governed by the current CUPE 2626 collective agreement; you can click here to find out more. The University of Ottawa embraces diversity and inclusion in the workplace. We are passionate about our people and committed to employment equity. We foster a culture of respect, teamwork and inclusion, where collaboration, innovation, and creativity fuel our quest for research and teaching excellence. While all qualified persons are invited to apply, we welcome applications from qualified Indigenous persons, raci