ench Requirements and Nature of Work: Nature du travail Donner des laboratoires, faire la correction du mi-session et des devoirs de groupe. \u00a0\u00a0Surveillance d'examen. Qualifications\u00a0n\u00e9cessaires Bonne compr\u00e9hension des concepts de gestion financi\u00e8re; Capacit\u00e9 \u00e0 appliquer des grilles de correction et \u00e0 fournir une r\u00e9troaction claire et structur\u00e9e; Capacit\u00e9 \u00e0 respecter des \u00e9ch\u00e9anciers stricts et \u00e0 g\u00e9rer efficacement sa charge de travail; Capacit\u00e9 d\u00e9montr\u00e9e \u00e0 r\u00e9soudre des probl\u00e8mes financiers avec pr\u00e9cision et efficacit\u00e9; Capacit\u00e9 \u00e0 interpr\u00e9ter des r\u00e9sultats financiers; Ma\u00eetrise d\u2019Excel; Moyenne cumulative minimale (C.G.P.A.) de 7,0; Note minimale de A- dans ADM2350 ou l\u2019\u00e9quivalent; Les candidats doivent \u00eatre en mesure de r\u00e9soudre des probl\u00e8mes financiers \u00e0 l\u2019aide de (1) Excel et (2) d\u2019une calculatrice financi\u00e8re approuv\u00e9e (CFA/LIFA), soit la Texas Instruments BAII+; Exp\u00e9rience en enseignement en ligne consid\u00e9r\u00e9e comme un atout; Exp\u00e9rience avec les plateformes de vid\u00e9oconf\u00e9rence (p. ex. Microsoft Teams) consid\u00e9r\u00e9e comme un atout; Bonne capacit\u00e9 d\u2019expression et de communication en fran\u00e7ais; \u00a0 Le travail doit \u00eatre fait en fran\u00e7ais; \u00a0 Commentaires La pr\u00e9f\u00e9rence sera accord\u00e9e aux candidats ayant les meilleures notes; La pr\u00e9f\u00e9rence sera accord\u00e9e aux candidats ayant d\u00e9j\u00e0 occup\u00e9 un poste d\u2019assistant(e) d\u2019enseignement ou de correcteur(trice) pour ce cours; La pr\u00e9f\u00e9rence sera accord\u00e9e aux candidats inscrits \u00e0 un programme de Telfer; Les candidats pr\u00e9s\u00e9lectionn\u00e9s seront invit\u00e9s \u00e0 une entrevue avec le professeur ou le coordonnateur du cours; Veuillez noter que les heures affich\u00e9es pourraient \u00eatre augment\u00e9es de 10 % \u00e0 30 % selon les inscriptions; Veuillez noter que vous devez avoir acc\u00e8s \u00e0 un ordinateur, une connexion Internet, un microphone et une cam\u00e9ra; Les heures du contrat peuvent \u00eatre r\u00e9parties diff\u00e9remment entre les t\u00e2ches, selon les besoins du professeur au cours de la session; Les candidats doivent \u00eatre situ\u00e9s \u00e0 Ottawa pour toute la dur\u00e9e du cours (\u00e0 l\u2019exception des jours f\u00e9ri\u00e9s officiels de l\u2019Universit\u00e9), y compris pour la correction de l\u2019examen final et le calcul des notes finales; Veuillez noter que la m\u00e9thode d\u2019enseignement ou de travail peut \u00eatre modifi\u00e9e pour des raisons de sant\u00e9 ou autres; \u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0 Additional Information and/or Comments: All University of Ottawa employees are required under provincial law to successfully complete all mandatory legislated training offered by the University. The list of training requirements may be modified by provincial law. If you are invited to continue the selection process, please notify us of any particular adaptive measures you might require. We may consult with the Health and Wellness sector of Human Resources, if needed. Any information you send us will be handled respectfully and in complete confidence. The hiring process will be governed by the current CUPE 2626 collective agreement; you can click here to find out more. The University of Ottawa embraces diversity and inclusion in the workplace. We are passionate about our people and committed to employment equity. We foster a culture of respect, teamwork and inclusion, where collaboration, innovation, and creativity fuel our quest for research and teaching excellence. While all qualified persons are invited to apply, we welcome applications from qualified Indigenous persons, racialized persons, persons with disabilities, women and LGBTQIA2S+ persons. The University is committed to creating and maintaining an accessible, barrier-free work environment. The University is also committed to working with applicants with disabilities requesting accommodation during the recruitment, assessment and selection processes. Applicants with disabilities may contact the academic unit to communicate the accommodation need. Prior to May 1, 2022, the University required all students, faculty, staff, and visitors (including contractors) to be fully vaccinated against Covid-19 as defined in Policy 129 \u2013 Covid-19 Vaccination. This policy was suspended effective May 1, 2022 but may be reinstated at any point in the future depending on public health guidelines and the recommendations of experts."}, "https://uottawa.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/uOttawa_External_Career_Site/job/Ottawa-ON/CUPE--Winter-2027---TA---ADM3308_JR40007": {"title": "CUPE -Winter 2027 - TA - ADM3308", "description": "Posted: 2026-10-19\nPart time\n\nPosting Reason: New Position Location where work is to be performed: Main Campus Session: 2027 Winter Semester | Trimestre d'hiver Faculty: \u00c9cole de gestion Telfer / Telfer School of Management Unit: Telfer School of Management_Students and Casuals Job Classification: Teaching Assistant/Demonstrator/Lab Monitor (CUPE) Posting Type: Cours pr\u00e9cis / Specific course Course Title: Business Data Mining Course Code: ADM3308 Section: Supervisor name (if known): Bijan Raahemi Date Posted (YYYY/MM/DD): 2026/10/19 Applications must be received BEFORE (YYYY/MM/DD): 2026/10/31 Description of tasks (hours): Unless specified below, specific allocation of hours to various tasks should be articulated in a description of work negotiated and signed by you and the supervising professor prior to the commencement of work. Recherche / Research:0 Pr\u00e9paration / Preparation:0 Contact avec \u00e9tudiants / Contact with Students:20 Correction - Notation / Grading:83 Surveillance / Proctoring:7 Formation / Training:0 Autre / Other:60 Number of positions: 2 Expected Enrolment: n/a Work Start Date: J